# The pipeline's own configuration — same reasoning as the block above, extended one
# step closer to the off switch. `/.claude/hooks/` above protects the guard *code*
# (pr-guard, migration-guard, schema-guard, residency-guard, instructions-audit), but
# those guards only run because settings.json registers them: deleting a few lines there
# disables every one of them while the guard files sit in the tree looking untouched, and
# nothing in CI checks whether the hooks are still wired. CLAUDE.md carries the six
# non-negotiables (§12.1); rules/ carries the path-scoped ones (minors'-data retention,
# service-role key handling, client privacy); skills/ defines what each pipeline stage
# must actually do — e.g. that /test runs pgTAP, walks UAT.md, and only records a green
# gate marker when the suite is genuinely green.
#
# None of these are covered by a CI check, so review is the only gate they have.
